wasn't afraid of taking on paraguay's  drug traffickers he led the country's  most important investigations against  organized crime and money laundering  it's a job that came with a lot of risk  and on tuesday he was shot three times  by hitman while honeymooning at a resort  on a colombian island near the coastal  city of cartagena  the killers arrived on jet skis moments  after pitch's wife journalist claudia  aguilera announced on social media they  were expecting a baby  the killing has shocked both colombia  and paraguay  it is very painful very hard i spoke  with colombian president ivan duque on  the phone and he promised me that he  would give us all his support to solve  the case to look for those responsible  i've also spoken with the north american  government about this who will support  us through colombia now i'm going to  visit the attorney general  colombia's national police sent homicide  investigators to cartagena a police  delegation from paraguay will assist the  investigation  we have information that is being  collected in urgent efforts and which is  confidential which will help us to  identify those responsible for this  regrettable occurrence  hours later the police released two  pictures of one of the alleged killers  pitchy was seen as an incorruptible  prosecutor in one of the most corrupt  countries in latin america but his  success in high-profile drug and money  laundering cases brought him powerful  enemies his death shows the reach of  paraguay's drug mafias and their  connections in colombia alessandra piety  al jazeera bogota
 

